  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Litty Mol John vs The Station House Officer on 28 January, 2026 Author: Bechu Kurian Thomas Bench: Bechu Kurian Thomas Wp(C) No. 25363 Of 2025 1 2026:Ker:6937 In The High Court Of Kerala At Ernakulam Present The Honourable Mr. Justice Bechu Kurian Thomas Wednesday, The 28Th Day Of January 2026 / 8Th Magha, 1947 Wp(C) No. 25363 Of 2025 Petitioner : Litty Mol John Aged 38 Years D/O John, Kunnapalliyil House, Erattayar P.O., Kalkoonthal, Idukki, Pin - 685 514 By Advs. Sri.Jomy K. Jose Shri.Muhammed Anshif T.K. Respondents : 1 The Station House Officer Kattappana Police Station, Kattappana P.O., Idukki, Pin - 685508 2 The District Police Chief Idukki, Office Of The District Police Chief, Painavi P.O., Idukki, Pin - 685603 Litty Mol John vs The Station House Officer on 28 January, 2026 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/126571815/ 1 3 Anand Urumbolil Age And Fathers Name Unknown, Urumbolipady Valiya Thovala P.O., Idukki, Pin - 685514 Wp(C) No. 25363 Of 2025 2 2026:Ker:6937 4 Sabu Urumbolil Age And Fathers Name Unknown Urumbolipady Valiya Thovala P.O., Idukki, Pin - 685514 5 Francis Urumbolil Age And Fathers Name Unknown Urumbolipady Valiya Thovala P.O., Idukki, Pin - 685514 Sri. Rajeev Jyothish George, Government Pleader",
    "facts": "The business is claimed to be conducted in Building No.7-816 of Erattayar Grama Panchayath in accordance with the rules and regulations. Petitioner contends that she has obtained all the licences required under law and relies upon Ext.P1 to Ext.P3. According to the petitioner, respondents 3 to 5 are obstructing the conduct of business as they are competitors in the same field of business. It is in such circumstance that the petitioner approached this Court seeking police protection after the police failed to act in accordance with law pursuant to Ext.P5 request. 3. Though notice to respondents 3 to 5 had been served, none appears on his behalf.",
